  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "One gallery, several catalogs",
      "items": [
        "Each repo generates its own Registry v1 catalog and publishes it at /registry/ on its own site",
        "The gallery lists Cronsole's catalog plus every catalog in EXTERNAL_SOURCES, read live from each host",
        "A change in a catalog repo reaches the gallery on that repo's next deploy, with no Cronsole release"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "The automation that grows it",
      "items": [
        "An automated weekly job adds a few extended templates to bundled.ts and packs.ts, regenerates registry/ and opens a PR",
        "Merging is what publishes, so a batch that is not green opens as a draft",
        "It reads the other catalogs to judge overlap, never uses their id prefixes and never writes to them",
        "The other catalogs grow when their repos gain a recipe or job; their templates are generated, not written"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "What reaches your install",
      "items": [
        "Only Cronsole's own core templates arrive by themselves, through catalogSync",
        "Everything else, including every external catalog, arrives when you download it and import it",
        "Imported rows are managed: false, so catalog sync never prunes them"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Rules for external catalogs",
      "items": [
        "Never Built-in: the gallery forces core to false for any catalog but Cronsole's",
        "Downloads fetch the exact bytes from the host the entry came from; only the app's opt-in catalog source checks sha256",
        "A catalog that fails to load is named on the page; Cronsole's own still renders",
        "Cronsole's catalog wins an id collision, so external ids carry their repo's prefix"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Keeping them honest",
      "items": [
        "Each repo's CI fails when its generated catalog is stale, and its daily drift check hashes every served file",
        "Front door drift loads every catalog the gallery lists: the CORS header, every sha256, no id clash with Cronsole",
        "It also probes every public org homepage for /registry/ and fails on a catalog the gallery does not list",
        "Recipe READMEs link to their gallery pages from a generated block; Edge-Radar and Edge Spectrum link from their docs"
      ]
    }
  ]
